  "message670": "How these phases work",
  "message671": "The early ratio is the assumption above. The later ratio takes effect immediately after the early phase, then stays fixed until the terminal fade begins. Timing must satisfy 1 ≤ early end < later end < terminal year ≤ 30. The fade interpolates capital intensity (1 ÷ sales / capital), not the ratio itself. In simulation, both authored ratios move proportionally with the same sales / capital draw. Turning this option off restores the existing capital path and keeps these phase inputs available.",
