  "model50": "Independent interim margin path",
  "model51": "Margin moves from normalized starting EBIT to the interim target, holds through the selected decline-start year, then reaches the terminal target in its independent terminal year and holds. Growth and capital efficiency keep their existing calendars; extending margin timing does not delay either. The explicit forecast continues until all active transitions have finished. Terminal ROIC and snapshot capital claims remain separate judgments.",
  "model52": "One terminal-margin draw shifts interim and terminal margins by the same percentage-point difference. Starting normalized EBIT is unchanged. Infeasible draws are rejected, never clipped.",
  "model53": "One sales / capital draw scales both early and later ratios proportionally; dates stay fixed, and terminal capital intensity follows the sampled mature margin. No extra capital-efficiency draw is added.",
  "model54": "Early and later incremental sales / capital are independent analyst assumptions. Later capital intensity fades to (1 + stable growth) × mature margin × (1 − tax) / terminal ROIC on its own calendar. Growth and margin keep their existing timelines; the forecast continues until all active transitions end. The displayed marginal-return proxy is not ROIC on accumulated invested capital.",
